    connectivity: 1 component (8-connected); may be >1 in 4-connected
  markers:
    count: 1-2, each a single pixel of a distinct non-source color
    alignment: each marker shares exactly one row OR exactly one column with exactly one source pixel (never both); the other axis has 0 matches
    gap: 4-9 empty cells between the anchor source pixel and the marker
    direction: marker can be left/right (row-aligned) or above/below (col-aligned) of anchor
  no_overlap: source, all reflected copies, and markers must not overlap; all copies fit within grid
  output:
    keep source and markers unchanged
    for each marker, reflect the entire source shape across the midpoint between the anchor pixel and the marker, recolor to marker color
    row-aligned marker => horizontal reflection (flip columns, same rows offset); col-aligned marker => vertical reflection (flip rows, same columns offset)
    each reflected copy has same pixel count as source

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H x W in [11-14] x [11-16]
    2. Generate an asymmetric source shape (6-9 pixels, bbox 3-4 x 3-5, 8-connected, density ~0.44-0.58)
    3. Choose 1-2 marker count; for each marker pick a reflection axis (horizontal or vertical)
